hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17681","He said: I read to 'Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, freedman of 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from Busr ibn Sa'id, that Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani sent him to Abu Juhaym asking him what he heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning one who passes in front of a praying person, what is upon him. Abu al-Juhaym said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the one passing in front of a praying person knew what is upon him, standing forty would be better for him than passing in front of him. Abu al-Nadr said: I do not know whether he said forty days, or forty months, or forty years."
